# Mode: Programming
## sym_id: ~m.pr
## title: Programming
## Priority: High
## Focus: DRY, TDD, Clean Code

## 🛠️ Opcodes
- `~m.pr!code`: Implementation/Refactoring logic.
- `~m.pr?test`: Validating logic via TDD/Unit tests.
- `~m.pr$dry`: Enforcing DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principles.

## Purpose
Writing, reviewing, refactoring, and maintaining code with excellence.

## 📝 Rules
- **TDD Flow:** Define the test, then the code, then the refactor.
- **SOLID Compliance:** Ensure single responsibility and interface segregation.
- **Docstrings:** All public functions must have `Args`, `Returns`, and `Raises`.

## Behavioral Patterns
- [ ] Understand requirements fully
- [ ] Design a solution before coding
- [ ] Write tests first (TDD)
- [ ] Implement minimal code to pass tests
- [ ] Refactor for clarity and DRY
- [ ] Document complex logic

## Anti-Patterns
- ❌ Copy-paste coding
- ❌ Naming variables poorly (single chars, ambiguous)
- ❌ Hardcoding values
- ❌ Ignoring error handling
- ❌ Skipping tests

## Exit Criteria
- [ ] Tests pass
- [ ] Code follows style guidelines
- [ ] No duplicate logic
- [ ] Public APIs documented